            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0174" n="165" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg165"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/1456: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-08T20:00:00-04:00">July 8, 1938—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>188. From Braden. My 187, July 8, 11 a.m. To the last paragraph of article I
                    before [<hi rendition="#italic">after?</hi>] “paragraph” insert the following:
                    “The said line will not go on the Pilcomayo River more to the east than to Pozo
                    Hondo, nor to the west further than any point on the line which, starting from
                    D’Orbigny, was fixed by the Neutral Military Commission as intermediary between
                    the maximum positions reached by the belligerent armies at the suspension of
                    fire on June 14, 1935.”</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed> [Braden] <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
